= Cell Biology True or False Quiz

_Grade 9 Science_

*Name:* #line(length: 60%) *Date:* #line(length: 25%)

*Instructions:* Read each statement. Write *T* if the statement is true or *F* if it is false. For each false statement, you may rewrite the statement so that it becomes true.

+ The cell membrane controls which substances enter and leave the cell. #h(1fr) T / F #line(length: 3cm)
+ Plant cells have a cell wall made of cellulose. #h(1fr) T / F #line(length: 3cm)
+ Mitochondria are the site of photosynthesis in plant cells. #h(1fr) T / F #line(length: 3cm)
+ The nucleus contains most of the cell's DNA. #h(1fr) T / F #line(length: 3cm)
+ Prokaryotic cells have a nucleus surrounded by a membrane. #h(1fr) T / F #line(length: 3cm)
+ Ribosomes are the site of protein synthesis. #h(1fr) T / F #line(length: 3cm)
+ Animal cells usually have one large central vacuole. #h(1fr) T / F #line(length: 3cm)
+ Osmosis is the movement of water across a membrane from a region of high water concentration to a region of low water concentration. #h(1fr) T / F #line(length: 3cm)
+ Lysosomes contain digestive enzymes. #h(1fr) T / F #line(length: 3cm)
+ The cytoplasm is the jelly-like fluid that fills the cell and holds the organelles. #h(1fr) T / F #line(length: 3cm)
+ Chloroplasts contain chlorophyll. #h(1fr) T / F #line(length: 3cm)
+ Diffusion requires the cell to use energy from ATP. #h(1fr) T / F #line(length: 3cm)

#pagebreak()

= Answer Key

+ *T.* The selectively permeable membrane regulates transport into and out of the cell.
+ *T.* Cellulose gives the plant cell wall its strength and rigidity.
+ *F.* Mitochondria release energy through cellular respiration. Photosynthesis takes place in chloroplasts.
+ *T.* The DNA is stored in the nucleus, with a small amount also found in mitochondria and chloroplasts.
+ *F.* Prokaryotic cells have no membrane-bound nucleus. Their DNA sits in the nucleoid region.
+ *T.* Ribosomes read genetic instructions and assemble amino acids into proteins.
+ *F.* Plant cells usually have one large central vacuole. Animal cells have several small vacuoles, if any.
+ *T.* Water moves down its concentration gradient across the membrane.
+ *T.* Lysosomes break down waste materials, damaged organelles, and food particles.
+ *T.* The cytoplasm supports the organelles and is where many cell reactions occur.
+ *T.* Chlorophyll absorbs light energy for photosynthesis.
+ *F.* Diffusion is a passive process and does not require energy from ATP. Movement by active transport does require ATP.